      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "It is recommended today that care for people with diabetes should be given in the community. New initiatives are being set up to deliver that care, and new treatments are constantly being developed, such as insulin analogues that provide an opportunity for patients to adjust their insulin regimen to suit their lifestyle. National initiatives in diabetes care are aiming to reduce inequalities in care."},
